NAME
       rev - reverse the characters of each line

SYNOPSIS
       rev [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
       rev prints every line with its characters in reverse order. A common
       trick is to take the last field of a line: reverse, cut the first
       field, reverse again.

EXAMPLES
           echo hello | rev
           echo /srv/web/index.html | rev | cut -d/ -f1 | rev

SEE ALSO
       tac(1), cut(1)
